<%
    // The outcome of a rejudge, read from the redirect's query string.
    //
    // SHOWN RATHER THAN ONLY LOGGED because the outcome is not always success: a
    // regrouping can be recorded while the new weighing fails, and an admin who is
    // not told would see an unchanged number and assume the tool ignored them.
    //
    // Every value below is escaped by the template engine, so a model's own words
    // in a note cannot become markup, and a thrown error's message is inert.
%>
<% if (typeof notice !== 'undefined' && notice) { %>
    <% if (notice.error) { %>
        <div class="problem"><%= notice.error %></div>
    <% } %>
    <% if (notice.rejudged) { %>
        <%# THE SUBJECT COMES FROM THE VIEW. "The answer was regrouped" is wrong on the
            roadmap, where the admin rejudged a process, and the same mechanism serving
            two places must not describe itself in the language of one of them. %>
        <div class="notice">
            <%= subject %> was <%= notice.rejudged %>.
            <% if (notice.weighed) { %>
                A new score was produced.
            <% } else if (notice.note) { %>
                <%= notice.note %>
            <% } %>
            <%# A MOVE CHANGES TWO PROCESSES, and the admin is looking at one of them.
                Without this the other one changes silently, and its score may have
                gone, which is exactly the sort of quiet change a reader must be told
                about rather than discover. The name is a model-supplied string and
                goes through the escaping tag like every other value here. %>
            <% if (notice.moved) { %>
                It moved out of &ldquo;<%= notice.moved %>&rdquo;.
                <%# THE REASON REPLACES THE SUMMARY, NOT BOTH. When the source could
                    not be reweighed, `leftNote` already explains that it now has no
                    score and why; saying it twice read as two separate faults. With no
                    note, the short clause is the whole story. %>
                <% if (notice.leftWeighed) { %>
                    That process was reweighed as well.
                <% } else if (notice.leftNote) { %>
                    <%= notice.leftNote %>
                <% } else { %>
                    That process now has no score.
                <% } %>
            <% } %>
        </div>
    <% } else if (notice.note) { %>
        <div class="notice"><%= notice.note %></div>
    <% } %>
<% } %>
